-            <p>Show that if \(x\) is attainable then \(\operatorname{rank}([A;\,x]) = \operatorname{rank}(A)\), using only Lemma 1.2 and Lemma 2.1.</p>
+            <p>Show that if \(x\) is attainable then \(\operatorname{rank}([A;\,x]) = \operatorname{rank}(A)\), using only Lemma 1.2 and Definition 1.3.</p>
             <details class="solution"><summary>Solution</summary>
               <p>If \(x\) is attainable, then \(x = \theta^\top A\) for some \(\theta\), so \(x \in \operatorname{row}(A)\) by Lemma 1.2. The row space of \([A;\,x]\) is \(\operatorname{row}(A) + \operatorname{span}(x)\), and since \(x\) lies in \(\operatorname{row}(A)\), this sum equals \(\operatorname{row}(A)\). Equal row spaces have equal dimension, so the ranks agree.</p>
             </details>
